**Plan: `--json` prints `buildRows()` rows straight, no table.**

```js
// cli.js
const args = argv.slice(1);
const json = args.includes('--json');
if (command !== 'report' || args.some((a) => a !== '--json')) { usage; return 1; }
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

One call to make. "Same data" is ambiguous. `toTable` drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, see [format.js:3](src/format.js:3). I would emit all six fields in JSON. Say the word if you want just the four table columns.

`format.js` and `report.js` stay untouched. Usage line becomes `usage: cli.js report [--json]`.
